    "full_readme_markdown": "# workspacer-toml\n\n`workspacer-toml` is a high-performance Rust library designed for sophisticated manipulation and validation of `Cargo.toml` files. This crate offers robust tools to ensure the correctness and integrity of your Cargo project metadata, leveraging advanced validation techniques and convenient access patterns.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Validation**: Provides comprehensive validation of `Cargo.toml` contents ensuring compliance with semantic versioning and the presence of essential fields.\n- **Access and Modification**: Facilitates intuitive interaction with components of `Cargo.toml`, allowing for retrieval and modification of entries such as authors, edition, and dependencies.\n- **Asynchronous and Synchronous Operations**: Supports both async and sync methods for creating instances and writing changes, suited for various runtime environments.\n- **Error Management**: Utilizes a refined error system to inform of missing fields, parse errors, and version invalidity.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Dependency\nAdd the following to your `Cargo.toml`:\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nworkspacer-toml = \"0.5.0\"\n```\n\n### Example\n```rust\nuse workspacer_toml::CargoToml;\nuse std::path::Path;\n\n#[tokio::main]\nasync fn main() -> Result<(), workspacer_toml::CargoTomlError> {\n    // Load and parse the Cargo.toml\n    let cargo_toml = CargoToml::new(Path::new(\"./Cargo.toml\")).await?;\n    \n    // Validate its structure and contents\n    cargo_toml.validate_integrity().await?;\n    \n    // Access and modify fields\n    if let Some(authors) = cargo_toml.get_package_authors()? {\n        println!(\"Authors: {:?}", authors);\n    }\n    \n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n## License\nThis project is licensed under either the MIT or Apache-2.0 license, at your option.\n\n## Contribution\nContributions are welcome, please follow standard open source contribution practices by forking the repository and submitting a pull request.\n\n## Repository\n[GitHub Repository](https://github.com/klebs6/klebs-general)\n",
